+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive coffee homepage with browser-encrypted delivery notes.
+
+## Build
+
+Install dependencies with `pnpm install`, then run `pnpm build`. Deploy `dist/` to an HTTPS static host. Web Crypto requires a secure context (HTTPS or localhost).
+
+## Delivery notes
+
+- **Hybrid (default):** independent P-256 ECDH and ML-KEM-768 shared secrets.
+- **Classical:** ephemeral P-256 ECDH with the local recipient's public key.
+- **Post-quantum:** ML-KEM-768 public-key encapsulation using `@noble/post-quantum`.
+- HKDF-SHA-256 derives a nonextractable AES-256-GCM key with a fresh 32-byte salt. A fresh 96-bit nonce is generated for every note, with a 128-bit authentication tag.
+- Fixed-order metadata binds the version, protection mode, recipient fingerprint, creation time, ephemeral public key, KEM ciphertext, salt, and nonce to both HKDF and GCM authenticated additional data.
+- Saving verifies independent recipient-side derivation and authenticated decryption before replacing an existing note.
+- Only the encrypted envelope is written to local storage. Unchecking device saving keeps the envelope in memory and removes an existing device note.
+- Note text is rendered using `textContent` when decrypted. Closing the dialog removes decrypted text from the DOM.
+
+## Demo boundary
+
+This repository has no authenticated delivery backend. It generates recipient keys locally, holds them in memory, and does not send notes anywhere. Reloading or closing the page loses the recipient keys, so old saved ciphertext can only be deleted or replaced. The interface labels this limitation.
+
+For a live delivery service, replace local recipient generation with authenticated, versioned recipient public keys, retain private keys only at the authorized recipient, and add authenticated order-bound ciphertext transport and retention controls. The demo fingerprint binds a note to the generated keys; it does not authenticate a delivery person's identity. Browser-side encryption does not protect against compromised page scripts or device access. Typed-array intermediates are cleared where practical; JavaScript strings and browser memory cannot be reliably erased.
+
+Coffee photos are loaded from Unsplash; fonts from Google Fonts; decorative avatars from Pravatar. External asset requests contain no delivery-note text. Icons are bundled locally from Lucide.
