+  showDialog('A little care for your privacy.', '<p><strong>Hybrid by default.</strong> P-256 key agreement and ML-KEM-768 encapsulation establish independent shared secrets. HKDF-SHA-256 derives an AES-256 key from both secrets and binds the key to the recipient and encryption metadata.</p><p><strong>Sealed in your browser.</strong> AES-256-GCM encrypts your note with a fresh nonce and authenticates its contents and metadata. Only the encrypted envelope is stored. Classical and post-quantum modes are also available.</p><p><strong>This is a local demo.</strong> Recipient keys stay in memory and expire when this page reloads or closes. Saved ciphertext cannot be reopened afterward. No note is sent to a delivery team, and no account or delivery service is connected.</p><p>A live service needs authenticated recipient public keys and secure recipient-side private-key management. This demo does not establish a delivery person’s identity. JavaScript strings cannot be reliably erased from memory.</p>');
